// Program metadata for yazi.
//
// kind=user → installed by the profile runner inside the chroot as the owning
// user via paru, with temp NOPASSWD sudo for seeding /etc/skel and /root.
// Seeds the ANSI-16 yazi theme (bundled under home/, kept byte-identical to the
// repo stow tree by a drift test) so a fresh non-stowing user gets a themed file
// manager; the repo copy stays hand-stowable. The program owns the yazi package
// — a Categorized-List entry may not also name a Program (exclusivity, ADR
// 0115), so yazi left core packages.shell for here. The theme is static ANSI-16
// (ADR 0132), so nothing is seed-only/gitignored (unlike kitty/zsh).

{
  "name": "yazi",
  "kind": "user",
  "description": "Yazi theme seeded fleet-wide, ANSI-16 palette-following (ADR 0132)."
}
